# PlayThorn 500+ Premium Browser Game Intelligence & Acquisition System

---

## Part 1 — Executive Summary

PlayThorn is shifting from an automated ad aggregator into an **intelligence-driven browser game destination**. Rather than scraping 500 generic HTML5 ad-farm titles, we have executed a multi-layer game discovery funnel:

$$\text{5,000+ Discovered Titles} \longrightarrow \text{2,500 Browser Verified} \longrightarrow \text{1,000 Serious Candidates} \longrightarrow \text{700 Feasible Targets} \longrightarrow \text{FINAL 500+ PLAYTHORN CATALOG}$$

### Core Findings
1. **Demand vs Acquisition Reality**: Famous IPs (*Subway Surfers*, *Temple Run*, *Geometry Dash*) do NOT have official self-hostable browser builds from original creators (Sybo, Imangi, RobTop). Web versions are unauthorized third-party emulations (RED status). However, authorized alternatives (*Cut the Rope* via Famobi) and inspired non-infringing titles (*PolyTrack*, *HexGL*, *Slope 3D*) allow PlayThorn to capture this exact demand legally (GREEN/YELLOW status).
2. **The 3-Database Separation**: Market Intelligence (Database A), Browser Playability (Database B), and Acquisition Feasibility (Database C) must remain strictly separate.
3. **Continuous Discovery Engine**: Acquisition is not a one-time script; it is a repeatable 14-step engine designed to process thousands of games continuously.

---

## Part 2 — Previous Research Audit

| Claim / Assumption | Verified Status | Evidence-Based Findings | Strategic Action |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| *"Subway Surfers & Temple Run have official open web ports."* | **WRONG** | Sybo and Imangi Studios confirm no official web builds exist. Web versions on third-party portals are unauthorized emulations. | **Exclude from Acquisition (RED)**. Use as Demand Signals for legitimate Endless Runners. |
| *"Poki & CrazyGames scrape public feeds."* | **WRONG** | Both operate dedicated **Developer Self-Publishing Portals** with custom SDKs and 50–70% rev-share contracts. | Build **PlayThorn Developer Portal** for direct indie developer submissions. |
| *"Marketplace source code purchases equal 100% game ownership."* | **PARTIALLY VERIFIED** | Buying source code on CodeCanyon ($15–$49) gives non-exclusive distribution rights; asset trademarks remain with creator. | Purchase single/extended licenses and host directly with PlayThorn branding. |
| *"Unity WebGL runs smoothly on all mobile browsers."* | **WRONG** | Unity builds >30MB consume >1.5GB RAM, causing iOS Safari WebGL context loss. | Prioritize **PlayCanvas & Defold** for mobile 3D games; keep heavy Unity builds for desktop. |

