## Part 4 — Recognizable / Famous Titles & IP Matrix

We categorize every recognizable title into one of 5 IP Compliance Tiers:

| IP Compliance Tier | Definition | Example Games | PlayThorn Legal Status |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Tier A: Official Web Version** | Released natively by original developer for web. | *Cut the Rope* (Famobi), *Angry Birds Friends* | **GREEN** (Sign Publisher Deal) |
| **Tier B: Authorized License** | Licensed to distribution networks (Famobi, Softgames). | *Fireboy & Watergirl*, *Om Nom Run*, *Moto X3M* | **GREEN** (B2B Licensing) |
| **Tier C: Legitimate Inspired** | Original mechanics & graphics, no trademark infringement. | *PolyTrack*, *HexGL*, *Slow Roads*, *Basket Bros* | **GREEN / YELLOW** (Direct Licensing) |
| **Tier D: Unofficial Fan Port** | Unlicensed port using copyrighted code/assets. | *Eaglercraft* (Minecraft web), *Subway Surfers Web* | **RED (DO NOT ACQUIRE)** |
| **Tier E: Trademark Infringing** | Steals sprites, logos, or character names. | *Mario HTML5*, *Pokemon Web*, *Sonic Web* | **RED (DO NOT ACQUIRE)** |

