## Part 17 — 90-Day Execution Roadmap

```
MONTH 1: Self-Hosted Core & Infrastructure (30 Games)
├─ Week 1: Integrate 10 Top Open-Source MIT WebGL Games (HexGL, 2048, Hextris, BrowserQuest, A Dark Room, etc.)
├─ Week 2: Integrate 10 Additional WASM/3D Repos (OpenRA, Clumsy Bird 3D, MineClone, Space Company, TrackMania Web)
├─ Week 3: Upgrade Next.js Container with SharedArrayBuffer & Cross-Origin Isolation headers
└─ Week 4: QA testing, mobile touch controls verification, IndexedDB offline caching setup

MONTH 2: Commercial & Publisher Licensing (100 Games)
├─ Week 5-6: Purchase 25 Commercial Source Codes from CodeCanyon & Scirra Store
├─ Week 7-8: Sign B2B Agreements with Famobi & Softgames for 75 Premium Casual/Puzzle Titles

MONTH 3: Scale to 500+ & Developer Submission Portal (500+ Games)
├─ Week 9-10: Launch PlayThorn Developer Rev-Share Submission Portal for itch.io creators
├─ Week 11-12: Curate top 10% of GameDistribution B2B catalog to reach 500+ high-craft games
```

---

## Part 18 — Brutally Honest Risks & Unknowns

1. **IP Misconception Risk**: Viral mobile games (*Subway Surfers*, *Temple Run*) lack official web builds; attempting unauthorized web mirrors carries immediate DMCA take-down risks.
2. **Unity WASM RAM Spikes**: 30MB+ Unity builds trigger memory limits on low-end iOS devices; PlayCanvas/Phaser 3 must be used as mobile fallbacks.
3. **Cross-Origin Opener Policy**: Serving `COEP: require-corp` on Next.js enables `SharedArrayBuffer` for Godot 4/Unity WASM but requires all third-party iframe embeds to support COEP headers or credentialless modes.

